  <prompt>
    UAT round 3 (`notes/UAT-ROUND3-FEEDBACK.md` section C) refinements to the `CommunicationActions` PCF
    (`src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/`). Three items:

    C11-1 — increase the tool icon size to 20×20 to match OOB command-bar icons.
    C11-2 — for the ICON-ONLY buttons (the separator line, save-to-SharePoint, create event, etc.) make them
      RIGHT-ALIGNED in the toolbar (labelled buttons stay as they are; the icon-only cluster aligns right).
    C11-3 — Create Event / Create To Do / Link Invoice currently NAVIGATE to a new page/tab. They must open as
      MODALS instead. OWNER DECISION: FIRST check whether a CUSTOM Fluent v9 create dialog already exists for these
      flows (search the shared lib + solutions for existing Create*Wizard dialogs / modal launchers). IF a custom
      dialog exists, use it. IF NOT, open via OOB `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo(target, { target: 2, position: 1, ... })`
      (in-app centered dialog) — but route ALL THREE launches through a SINGLE launch seam/helper (e.g.
      `launchCreate(kind, ctx)`) so the OOB call can later be swapped for a custom Fluent dialog WITHOUT touching the
      button call sites. Preserve whatever record/context prefill the current navigation passes.
  </prompt>

  <goal>
    Toolbar icons are 20×20 (OOB parity); icon-only buttons are right-aligned; Create Event / Create To Do / Link
    Invoice open in a modal (existing custom dialog if present, else OOB `navigateTo target:2`) routed through one
    swappable launch seam. Existing send/attachment behavior (tasks 103/104) unchanged.
  </goal>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Tool icons render at 20×20 (verified in the manifest/styles + harness); matches OOB command-bar icon sizing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Icon-only buttons (separator, save-to-SharePoint, create-*, etc.) are right-aligned in the toolbar; any labelled buttons keep their placement.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Create Event / Create To Do / Link Invoice open as a MODAL (not a new page/tab). The task report states whether an existing custom dialog was found+used OR OOB `navigateTo target:2` was used; either way all three route through ONE launch seam/helper so the launch mechanism is swappable without editing call sites.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The record/context prefill previously passed to the navigation is preserved through the new modal launch (same entity/target + seeded values).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The W10 contact-autocomplete (103) and reply/forward-attachment (104) behavior is unaffected; existing EmailComposer wiring untouched.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build:prod` clean; jest updated/green (launch-seam dispatch + right-align/20px if testable); version bump all 5 locations (1.1.3 → 1.2.0); solution ZIP repacked + validated (type-66, apostrophe-free). NOTE: this control's `Solution/pack.ps1` writes `bin/` relative to CWD — run it from the `Solution/` dir (or harden to `$PSScriptRoot`) so the ZIP lands in `Solution/bin/`.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <constraints>
    <constraint>MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md: opening a record/create form → OOB `Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo` `{target:2}` is the sanctioned default; a custom Fluent dialog is acceptable if one already exists. Do NOT iframe-embed.</constraint>
    <constraint>Route all three create launches through ONE seam so OOB↔custom is swappable later (owner requirement).</constraint>
    <constraint>Do NOT regress tasks 103/104 (contact autocomplete, reply/forward attachments). ADR-021 Fluent v9 tokens; ADR-028 auth.</constraint>
    <constraint>Manifest description-keys generic + apostrophe-free; type-66 solution; follow /pcf-deploy. Prefer staying within `src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/**`; if a change must touch @spaarke/ui-components, STOP and report (avoids cross-batch races with W11 tasks 111/112 — though those are different controls, keep shared-lib untouched).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <notes>
    Read the CommunicationActions toolbar component + the current Create Event/To Do/Link Invoice handlers first to
    see how they navigate today (Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo pageType? openForm? a custom-page target?). The launch
    seam should wrap exactly that. Check `src/client/shared` + `src/solutions` for existing Create*Wizard modal
